// [expr.shift]/1: "the behavior is undefined" if the right operand is
// negative or "greater than or equal to the width of the promoted left
// operand". ch09 §9.1 makes a constant expression the same program as
// its runtime twin, so the evaluator says so rather than folding an
// undefined value into the program.
int main() {
    constexpr int too_wide = 1 << 32;
    return too_wide;
}
